{{also|grāfa|grāfā}}
==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkraːva/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|aːva|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|grafa||to dig|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*grabaną}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-strong|gróf|grófu|grafið}}

# to [[dig]]
# to [[bury]]
# to [[engrave]]
# to [[enquire]]
# {{context|impersonal|lang=is}} to [[suppurate]], to [[fester]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{is-conj-s6|gr|a|f}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|to bury}} {{l|is|greftra}}
* {{sense|to engrave}} {{l|is|skera}}
* {{sense|to enquire}} {{l|is|grafast}}, {{l|is|spyrja}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|grafa skurði}} (to trench)
* {{l|is|grafa undan}} (to undermine)

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|is|gröf}}

===Etymology 2===
From the verb {{term|grafa||to dig}}.

[[File:Kettenbagger CAT 325C LN.jpeg|thumb|A modern excavator.]]

====Noun====
{{is-noun|f|gröfu|gröfur}}

# an [[excavator]], a [[digger]]; {{gloss|large machine used to dig holes and trenches}}

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-f-w1|gr|a|f}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|keðjugrafa}} (trencher)
* {{l|is|traktorsgrafa}} (excavator loader)
* {{l|is|vökvagrafa}} (hydraulic excavator)
* {{l|is|vélgrafa}} (mechanical excavator)
* {{l|is|víragrafa}} (rope-operated excavator)

